   "source": [
    "# Math-Driven Linear Regression from Scratch\n",
    "\n",
    "## Professional AI Engineering Portfolio Project\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook implements **Linear Regression from first principles** using Python and NumPy.  \n",
    "The goal is to show how machine learning models connect to **linear algebra, calculus, statistics, optimization, and clean software engineering**.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is designed as a GitHub portfolio project for entry-level **AI Engineer / Machine Learning Engineer** applications."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "99560b1f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Problem Statement\n",
    "\n",
    "Linear regression is one of the most important foundational algorithms in machine learning.  \n",
    "In this project, we build a model that learns a relationship of the form:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$y = \\theta_0 + \\theta_1x + \\epsilon$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where:\n",
    "\n",
    "- $\\theta_0$ is the intercept or bias term\n",
    "- $\\theta_1$ is the feature weight or slope\n",
    "- $\\epsilon$ is random noise\n",
    "\n",
    "Instead of using a high-level model from scikit-learn, we implement the core algorithm ourselves."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1313b590",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Mathematical Foundation\n",
    "\n",
    "### Linear Algebra\n",
    "\n",
    "The prediction function is written in matrix form as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\hat{y} = X\\theta$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where:\n",
    "\n",
    "- $X$ is the feature matrix, including a column of ones for the bias term\n",
    "- $\\theta$ is the parameter vector\n",
    "- $\\hat{y}$ is the prediction vector\n",
    "\n",
    "### Calculus and Optimization\n",
    "\n",
    "We minimize the cost function:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$J(\\theta) = \\frac{1}{2m}\\sum_{i=1}^{m}(\\hat{y}^{(i)} - y^{(i)})^2$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The gradient is:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\nabla J(\\theta) = \\frac{1}{m}X^T(X\\theta - y)$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Gradient descent updates the parameters as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\theta := \\theta - \\alpha \\nabla J(\\theta)$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### Statistics\n",
    "\n",
    "We evaluate the model using MSE, RMSE, and $R^2$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d834a84f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0fcdeef5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Generate Synthetic Data\n",
    "\n",
    "We create a small dataset where the true relationship is approximately:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$y = 4 + 3x + \\epsilon$$\n",
    "\n",
    "This allows us to verify whether the model can learn parameters close to 4 and 3."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a49b7c7f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Generate synthetic data\n",
    "m = 100\n",
    "X = np.random.rand(m, 1)\n",
    "noise = np.random.randn(m, 1)\n",
    "y = 4 + 3 * X + noise\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Feature matrix shape: {X.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Target vector shape: {y.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "6fd40096",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
    "plt.scatter(X, y, alpha=0.75)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Feature x\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Target y\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Synthetic Regression Dataset\")\n",
    "plt.grid(True)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2328f709",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Implement Linear Regression from Scratch\n",
    "\n",
    "The functions below implement the model without using a machine learning framework."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3b9b3a38",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def add_bias_column(X):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Add a bias column of ones to the feature matrix.\"\"\"\n",
    "    return np.c_[np.ones((X.shape[0], 1)), X]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def predict(X, theta):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Return model predictions using y_hat = X @ theta.\"\"\"\n",
    "    return X @ theta\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def compute_cost(X, y, theta):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Compute J(theta) = 1/(2m) * sum((X theta - y)^2).\"\"\"\n",
    "    m = len(y)\n",
    "    errors = predict(X, theta) - y\n",
    "    return (1 / (2 * m)) * np.sum(errors ** 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def gradient_descent(X, y, theta, learning_rate=0.1, iterations=1000):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Optimize theta using batch gradient descent.\"\"\"\n",
    "    m = len(y)\n",
    "    cost_history = []\n",
    "\n",
    "    for _ in range(iterations):\n",
    "        gradients = (1 / m) * X.T @ (X @ theta - y)\n",
    "        theta = theta - learning_rate * gradients\n",
    "        cost_history.append(compute_cost(X, y, theta))\n",
    "\n",
    "    return theta, cost_history"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b0b14eae",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Train the Model\n",
    "\n",
    "We initialize parameters randomly, then use gradient descent to minimize the cost function."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "284831f5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_b = add_bias_column(X)\n",
    "theta_initial = np.random.randn(2, 1)\n",
    "learning_rate = 0.1\n",
    "iterations = 1000\n",
    "\n",
    "theta_optimized, cost_history = gradient_descent(\n",
    "    X_b,\n",
    "    y,\n",
    "    theta_initial,\n",
    "    learning_rate=learning_rate,\n",
    "    iterations=iterations,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Initial theta:\")\n",
    "print(theta_initial)\n",
    "print(\"\\nOptimized theta:\")\n",
    "print(theta_optimized)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "72edbd19",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
    "plt.plot(cost_history)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Iteration\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Cost J(theta)\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Training Loss During Gradient Descent\")\n",
    "plt.grid(True)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "73e450c5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Visualize the Fitted Regression Line"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e6c15076",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "y_pred = predict(X_b, theta_optimized)\n",
    "\n",
    "X_line = np.linspace(0, 1, 100).reshape(-1, 1)\n",
    "X_line_b = add_bias_column(X_line)\n",
    "y_line = predict(X_line_b, theta_optimized)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
    "plt.scatter(X, y, alpha=0.75, label=\"Training data\")\n",
    "plt.plot(X_line, y_line, linewidth=2, label=\"Fitted regression line\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Feature x\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Target y\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Linear Regression Fit\")\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.grid(True)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9840021c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Evaluate the Model"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0ec63ead",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def mean_squared_error(y_true, y_pred):\n",
    "    return np.mean((y_true - y_pred) ** 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def root_mean_squared_error(y_true, y_pred):\n",
    "    return np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(y_true, y_pred))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def r_squared(y_true, y_pred):\n",
    "    ss_res = np.sum((y_true - y_pred) ** 2)\n",
    "    ss_tot = np.sum((y_true - np.mean(y_true)) ** 2)\n",
    "    return 1 - (ss_res / ss_tot)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "mse = mean_squared_error(y, y_pred)\n",
    "rmse = root_mean_squared_error(y, y_pred)\n",
    "r2 = r_squared(y, y_pred)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Mean Squared Error: {mse:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Root Mean Squared Error: {rmse:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"R-squared: {r2:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "35f392b5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Residual Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Residuals help us inspect the model's errors:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$residual = y - \\hat{y}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "A good basic linear fit should have residuals scattered around zero without a strong visible pattern."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "26650e4b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "residuals = y - y_pred\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
    "plt.scatter(y_pred, residuals, alpha=0.75)\n",
    "plt.axhline(0, linestyle=\"--\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Predicted values\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Residuals\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Residual Plot\")\n",
    "plt.grid(True)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f364736a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Validate with the Normal Equation\n",
    "\n",
    "For linear regression, the closed-form solution is:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\theta = (X^TX)^{-1}X^Ty$$\n",
    "\n",
    "This provides a useful way to validate whether gradient descent learned similar parameters."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c92061c0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def normal_equation(X, y):\n",
    "    return np.linalg.pinv(X.T @ X) @ X.T @ y\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "theta_normal = normal_equation(X_b, y)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Theta from gradient descent:\")\n",
    "print(theta_optimized)\n",
    "print(\"\\nTheta from normal equation:\")\n",
    "print(theta_normal)\n",
    "print(\"\\nAbsolute difference:\")\n",
    "print(np.abs(theta_optimized - theta_normal))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5fa503ae",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
